\chapter{Enum Reflection}

\texttt{M\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}D\allowbreak{}S\allowbreak{}L\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}p} embeds the complete public header API of \href{https://github.com/Neargye/magic\_enum/tree/v0.9.8}{magic\_\allowbreak{}enum v0.9.8}: core reflection, flags, utility functions, fusion, constexpr switch dispatch, containers, stream operators, and formatting. It remains a self-contained C++20 header; no magic\_\allowbreak{}enum installation or link dependency is required.

The D module provides the same core reflection capability through native enum member discovery: names, values, entries, casts, indexing, adjacency, flags, compile-time dispatch/\allowbreak{}fusion and enum-indexed containers. Its customization uses \texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}O\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}s} and \texttt{E\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}N\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}s} UDAs, with no numeric search interval. Chapter 31 (Chapter 31) documents the D API and the language-specific differences. This chapter covers the embedded C++ API.

