Flags reflection enumerates named individual power-of-two bits, including high bits of unsigned underlying types. Zero and named composite constants are excluded from the flags value list. Zero is not a valid flag combination; unknown bits also fail validation. Global numeric range macros do not limit the flags scan.

\texttt{b\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}w\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}s} contains \texttt{\textasciitilde{}}, \texttt{|}, \texttt{\&}, \texttt{\textasciicircum{}}, \texttt{|\allowbreak{}=}, \texttt{\&\allowbreak{}=}, and \texttt{\textasciicircum{}\allowbreak{}=}. Import these operators explicitly where required; they are enabled for all enum types.

