\item{} \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}w\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{})} dispatches a runtime value into a compile-time constant. An unmatched value or unsupported handler receives a default-constructed result (or no action for \texttt{v\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}d}). The three-argument overload accepts an explicit fallback result. An explicit result type and reflection mode are supported by the upstream overloads.
\item{} \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}b\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{})} combines at least two reflected enum values into an optional, type-safe enum discriminator suitable for \texttt{s\allowbreak{}w\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}h}/\allowbreak{}\texttt{c\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}e}. All arguments must be reflected; the combined representation must fit in \texttt{s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}d\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}x\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}t}.
\item{} \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}x\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}=\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}1\allowbreak{})} and \texttt{e\allowbreak{}n\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}v\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{},\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}e\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}s\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}=\allowbreak{}\ \allowbreak{}1\allowbreak{})} return optionals when moving through the sorted value sequence. They return empty optionals for unknown values or out-of-bounds movement.
