Insertion prints reflected names, flag combinations, or the underlying integer for unknown values. It also accepts optional enum values. Extraction parses a name or flag combination and sets \texttt{f\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}b\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}t} on failure, leaving the destination value intact.

If the standard library provides \texttt{<\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}>} and \texttt{\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}c\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}l\allowbreak{}i\allowbreak{}b\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}o\allowbreak{}r\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}a\allowbreak{}t}, enum formatters are enabled automatically, including when \texttt{M\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}D\allowbreak{}S\allowbreak{}L\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}p} is included first. They support string formatting specifications and numeric fallback for unknown values. \texttt{\{\allowbreak{}f\allowbreak{}m\allowbreak{}t\allowbreak{}\}} support is enabled when its headers are included before \texttt{M\allowbreak{}u\allowbreak{}D\allowbreak{}S\allowbreak{}L\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}h\allowbreak{}p\allowbreak{}p}; it remains optional.

